findings.body:
**Concern.** `committedFixRound` treats the round as finished whenever any `session_done` follows the newest `fix_round`. It never checks whether a `steer` came after that `session_done`. A steer leaves the session in `awaiting-review`: `steerSession` only types into the pane and appends a `steer` event, and nothing on the `pup steer` path moves the state back to `running`. So after a steer the worker is busy again, but the row still qualifies. `newestGateRefused` also returns `false` as soon as it meets a `steer`, so the `!gateRefused` guard in `dashboardSession` drops away at the moment the worker resumes.

**Trigger.** The conductor runs `pup merge <id> --pr` on a finished fix round, and the gate refuses it on flagged debt. `refuseGate` writes only a `gate_result` and no `merge`, so the round stays open. That line's answer is `pup steer <id> "..."`, and the operator or the conductor sends it. On the next `pup status`, `gateRefused` is false, the newest mark is still the `fix_round`, the old `session_done` is still found, and the branch is still past the pin. The inbox therefore prints `fix committed <age of the old session_done> ago, awaiting re-gate` with `pup merge <id> --pr`. A plain operator steer to a fix-committed session hits the same path.

**Wrong result.** `needOf` checks `fixCommitted` before the `!gating` guard, so the line shows even while the conductor runs. The conductor acts on `pup status`, so it is told to re-gate a branch the worker is still changing. ADR 0102 (`docs/adr/0102-while-the-project-s-conductor-runs-a-session.md`) says "a steer or a new `session_done` after the refusal hands it back to the conductor". A premature re-gate holds the merge lock and runs every stage on a half-done fix. The age also counts from the old `session_done`, so the line looks overdue the moment it reappears. No test puts a steer after the round's `session_done`.

```ts
const at = newestFirst.findIndex((row) => marks.includes(row.type));
const done = newestFirst.slice(0, at).find((row) => row.type === 'session_done');
...
const isOpenRound = newestFirst[at]?.type === 'fix_round' && done !== undefined;
```

